  "body": "This revision presents an attributed verification of the known focal-inversion area-product theorem. For strictly nested nondegenerate confocal ellipses, the product of signed orbit area and signed unit-focus-inverse chord-polygon area is constant when the **least collision period is N=4n**, for either original focus and every admitted coprime winding, including stars. The two inverse areas agree; reversal preserves the product, and r traversals of an admitted primitive cycle multiply it by r squared.\n\nThe original arXiv:2004.12497v11 Table 9 does not explicitly impose least period. The unrestricted repeated-list reading is false: connected least-period-three orbits repeated four times give length-twelve product difference -20 sqrt(6)/9. [Ferudun's preprint, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23093706](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23093706), already proves the exact positive theorem and states the repetition limitation. Local/cyclic Jacobi identities and generalized Landen methods are classical. No theorem/method novelty, firstness, causal independence, simultaneity, or current-openness claim is made.\n\nThe current complex argument retains its mathematical body with an explicit scope and attribution preface. The alternate [published telescoping verification note source](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/main/draft_pr_publication_program_20260930/audits/pr207_5100044/publication_package_v1/focal_inversion_area.tex) is frozen and published as [10.5281/zenodo.23428090](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23428090). The original 20-file, 61,131-byte [submitted archive](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/tree/main/draft_pr_publication_program_20260930/audits/pr207_5100044/submitted_snapshot) is preserved unchanged; these later corrections are dated 16 October 2026.\n\nCurrent `verify.py` provides finite exact algebra certificates and `independent_review/independent_check.py` propagates Euclidean reflected rays for numerical diagnostics. They use explicit checks under Python optimization, pinned dependencies, fresh current outputs, and exclusive result-file creation. They do not certify the whole analytic manuscript or provide interval bounds. Historical assertion-only scripts and their original receipts remain in the archive.\n\nThe preserved ledger cells remain `claimed_solved`, `1/5`; model/effort and author-turn counts are unverified, and three commits are not counted as three author work turns. The scoped mathematics and attributed editorial route have passed their recorded audits. Two new independent AI whole-package reviews were accepted by Root with no required repairs; this remains unrefereed and has no conventional human peer review or proof-assistant formalization. **Publication ready: true.** AI tools were used extensively; this is unrefereed and has no conventional human peer-review or proof-assistant certification.\n\nPublished verification note: [10.5281/zenodo.23428090](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23428090). The exact four-file deposit and tracker 'Math Puzzles'!A134:D134 were verified from actual service readbacks. The earlier DOI above belongs to Ferudun. Native adoption and PR merger are separately verified by actual Root receipts; this publication update alone makes no merger or overall-goal completion claim.\n",
